   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Say hello",
   "texto": [
    "**Bonjour** is the usual greeting during the day, in both formal and informal situations. In the evening **bonsoir** is usually used.",
    "**Salut** is informal and serves to greet and say goodbye. To say goodbye in a formal situation: **au revoir**.",
    "In French it is of good education to add **madame** or **monsieur**: **Bonjour, madame**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "You and vous",
   "texto": [
    "**Tu** is «You»: it is used with friends, family and children. **Vous** is «You» and also «You.». With an adult you don't know, **vous** is a safe and courteous option; customs may vary according to relationship and context.",
    "To say your name: **Je m'appelle Léa** (my name is Léa).",
    "To ask: **Comment tu t'appelles ?** (informal) or **Comment vous vous appelez ?** (formal).",
    "Writing detail: in French a space is left before **?** and **!**."
   ]
